 # Sparse Grid Volume Rendering (Foreground)
 
-Also called: Plenoxel Ray Tracing (Forward)
+Also called: Fused Sparse Voxel Volume Rendering (CuVol), JNeRF volume rendering, Plenoxel Ray Tracing (Forward)
 
 ## Overview
-Sparse Grid Volume Rendering (Foreground) is a CUDA-based volume rendering method that traces rays through a sparse voxel grid to compute final color and log-transmittance using volume rendering with spherical harmonics (SH) coefficients [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from its siblings by explicitly managing warp-level parallelism for SH basis evaluation and accumulation, utilizing shared memory for warp-local data to minimize global memory traffic, and employing early termination based on transmission thresholds [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [CUDA Ray Marching (IDDR-NGP Backend)](5788-cuda-ray-marching-iddr-ngp-backend.md) which uses hash encoding, or [Sparse Packed Radiance Field Tracer](13126-sparse-packed-radiance-field-tracer.md) which may use different interpolation schemes, this method relies on trilinear interpolation over a sparse connectivity structure [S1, S2, unofficial].
